1
00:00:00,111 --> 00:00:01,941
(Penny:)I don't know, Sheldon.

2
00:00:02,113 --> 00:00:04,533
(Penny:)Are you Star Wars?

3
00:00:05,783 --> 00:00:09,243
(Sheldon:)How can one person be a whole movie?

4
00:00:09,704 --> 00:00:12,334
(Penny:)Okay, I give up.
Can we just do something else?

5
00:00:12,498 --> 00:00:13,828
(Sheldon:)Fine.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,080
(Sheldon:)I was Spock.

7
00:00:20,631 --> 00:00:23,221
(Sheldon:)Are you and Leonard
friends with benefits?

8
00:00:23,968 --> 00:00:25,178
(Raj:)What?

9
00:00:25,344 --> 00:00:27,434
(Sheldon:)Are you and Leonard
friends with benefits?

10
00:00:27,597 --> 00:00:28,977
Where did that even come from?

11
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,310
(Penny:)- Did he say we were?
- No, Leonard said nothing.

12
00:00:31,475 --> 00:00:35,605
(Sheldon:)But who knows what goes on over here when
he pretends your mail was misdelivered?

13
00:00:36,898 --> 00:00:38,778
(Penny:)Just mail, no benefits.

14
00:00:39,442 --> 00:00:40,772
(Sheldon:)I see.

15
00:00:40,943 --> 00:00:42,573
(Penny:)Why are you asking?

16
00:00:42,737 --> 00:00:45,577
(Sheldon:)I'm curious about
the whole social construct.

17
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:49,700
(Sheldon:)On its face, the idea of satisfying
one's sexual appetite...

18
00:00:49,869 --> 00:00:51,699
(Sheldon:)Assuming one is afflicted with such.

19
00:00:51,871 --> 00:00:56,251
(Sheldon:)...without emotional entanglement,
that seems imminently practical.

20
00:00:56,417 --> 00:01:03,027
(Sheldon:)What I've observed, however,
is Howard Wolowitz crying like a little girl.

